Additional Terms: Liquidated Damages for Unauthorised Commercial Use

The following terms supplement the Business Source License above and apply to
any use of the Licensed Work that violates the Additional Use Grant.

1. Nature of Damages

   The Licensor has invested substantial time, original research, and
   intellectual effort in developing the Licensed Work — including its
   classification heuristics, adapter protocols, catalog design, and the
   harness-engineering methodology it embodies. Unauthorised commercial use
   causes harm that is difficult to quantify precisely. The parties therefore
   agree that the amounts in section 2 constitute a reasonable pre-estimate
   of damages and not a penalty.

2. Liquidated Damages — Tiered by Organisation Size

   Any person or legal entity that makes commercial use of the Licensed Work
   without a valid commercial licence shall owe the Licensor, upon demand,
   the GREATER of (a) the tier-based amount or (b) the revenue-based amount
   defined below, per production instance or deployment unit, per calendar
   month of unauthorised use, retroactive to the date on which commercial
   use first commenced.

   (a) Tier-based amounts:

       Tier 1 — Startup (fewer than 15 employees or annual revenue below
                USD 1,000,000 / BRL 5,500,000):
                USD 25,000 / BRL 137,500 per instance per month.

       Tier 2 — Growth (15–250 employees or annual revenue between
                USD 1,000,000 and USD 50,000,000 / BRL 5,500,000–275,000,000):
                USD 50,000 / BRL 275,000 per instance per month.

       Tier 3 — Enterprise (more than 250 employees or annual revenue above
                USD 50,000,000 / BRL 275,000,000):
                USD 150,000 / BRL 825,000 per instance per month.

   (b) Revenue-based amount:

       15% (fifteen percent) of the infringing party's gross monthly revenue
       directly or indirectly attributable to the product, service, or
       workflow that incorporates the Licensed Work, for each month of
       unauthorised use.

   Where both USD and BRL amounts are asserted in the same proceeding, the
   Licensor shall recover whichever denomination yields the higher amount at
   the prevailing exchange rate on the date of the demand, not both.

3. Minimum Per-Action Damages

   In addition to the recurring amounts above, the infringing party shall be
   liable for:

   (a) A minimum lump sum of USD 150,000 / BRL 825,000 per enforcement
       action, regardless of duration, as compensation for investigation,
       legal preparation, reputational harm, and lost licensing opportunity.

   (b) All reasonable legal fees and costs incurred by the Licensor,
       including attorney fees on a full-indemnity basis.

   (c) Disgorgement of all profits derived from the unauthorised use.

4. Wilful Infringement Multiplier

   If the Licensor demonstrates that the infringing party had actual knowledge
   of this License and proceeded with commercial use regardless, all amounts
   in sections 2 and 3 shall be multiplied by three (3×).

5. Jurisdiction and Governing Law

   The Licensor may bring an action in any of the following, at sole election:

   (a) The courts of Brazil — Foro Central da Comarca de São Paulo,
       Estado de São Paulo — governed by Brazilian law (Lei 9.610/98,
       Lei 9.609/98, and the Brazilian Civil Code).

   (b) Any court of competent jurisdiction in the country or US state where
       the infringing party is incorporated, domiciled, or operates its
       principal place of business.

   (c) Any court of competent jurisdiction in the State of New York, USA,
       governed by New York law and the US Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 101
       et seq.).

   The infringing party consents to jurisdiction in each of the above forums
   and waives any objection based on inconvenient forum.

6. Good Faith Cure

   If an infringing party (i) ceases all unauthorised commercial use within
   30 days of receiving written notice from the Licensor, and (ii) pays all
   accrued liquidated damages for the full period of infringement within 60
   days of such notice, the Licensor may, at sole discretion, waive the
   minimum lump sum in section 3(a) and the wilful multiplier in section 4.
   This cure provision may only be exercised once per legal entity and does
   not apply if the infringement continued after a prior notice.

7. Severability

   If any provision of these Additional Terms is found wholly or partially
   unenforceable under applicable law, that provision shall be enforced to
   the maximum extent permissible, and all remaining provisions continue in
   full force and effect.

8. Entire Agreement

   These Additional Terms and the Business Source License 1.1 above together
   constitute the entire agreement between the Licensor and any user of the
   Licensed Work with respect to the subject matter hereof, and supersede all
   prior representations, agreements, and understandings.

